From c5c2caddff06964611a7ae08e6406df3c3f3bcd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <virajslko@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:54:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 06/18] audio: size resampled buffers by the output's channel
 count
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With FFmpeg's channel-layout API (FF_API_OLD_CHANNEL_LAYOUT off, FFmpeg >= 7)
AudioStream::resampleAudio sized its output buffer — and the byte count it
returns — from the INPUT's channel count, while the resampler converts to
the driver's layout. A mono sound played on a stereo output (the SDL
driver's and the host driver's default) made swr_convert write two
channels into a one-channel buffer: heap corruption, "double free or
corruption" on a later free, and half-length audio in between.

Use the output's channel count, matching the layout the resampler was set
up with in the constructor (the old-API branch already did).

Reproduced by patches/lwe/tests/host_api_test.cpp
host_pull_mixes_scene_sound_at_unity_gain (livepaper repo): a scene with one
looping mono WAV aborted on the first pull.

Origin: ours
Why: any scene with a mono sound crashed the scene worker's process (found by the host driver's test)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/core/WallpaperEngine/Audio/AudioStream.cpp | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Audio/AudioStream.cpp b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Audio/AudioStream.cpp
index 768353f..27ea6da 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Audio/AudioStream.cpp
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Audio/AudioStream.cpp
@@ -491,7 +491,20 @@ int AudioStream::resampleAudio (uint8_t* out_buf, const int out_size) {
 
     out_nb_channels = av_get_channel_layout_nb_channels (out_channel_layout);
 #else
-    out_nb_channels = this->getContext ()->ch_layout.nb_channels;
+    // the OUTPUT's channel count (the layout the resampler was set up with in the constructor), not
+    // the input's: a mono sound resampled for a stereo output writes two channels, and a buffer
+    // sized for one overflows the heap
+    switch (this->m_audioContext.getChannels ()) {
+	case 1:
+	    out_nb_channels = 1;
+	    break;
+	case 2:
+	    out_nb_channels = 2;
+	    break;
+	default:
+	    out_nb_channels = 3; // AV_CH_LAYOUT_SURROUND
+	    break;
+    }
 #endif
     ret = av_samples_alloc_array_and_samples (
 	&resampled_data, &out_linesize, out_nb_channels, out_nb_samples, this->m_audioContext.getFormat (), 0
